https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QS-YZlJLCbM  (Capo 0)

TIP:  The intro looks strange but is very simple.  Start with plucking three notes:  open 3rd string (g), then the 2nd string/1st fret (c), and the 3rd string/2nd fret (a) and strum the (Gadd).  (Notes may or may not transpose.) 

TIP:  Still talking about the intro, to go from (Gadd) to (G-) just lift off the bottom two strings.  To play the (Em/F) just add your pinky to the 1st string/2nd fret.  "(Roll)" after the (C) chord means roll your index finger down to cover the 1st string/first fret.  To play the (D4) just add your pinky to the 1st string/3rd fret (no need to remove your index finger).  Again, it looks complicated but it’s really simple.  If transposing, play the root chord and add the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  In the verse there's a (Bm).  You can play an (Em) instead if you'd rather and it will sound just fine.
    

